            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# wef-notch 0.6.1

**A finished countdown waits for you.** When a countdown reaches zero, the
notch opens to the bar with `Countdown · done · 25:00` and now stays that way
until you click it, however long you were away, instead of going after four
seconds. A click on the words opens the Timer tab; a click anywhere else on
the bar opens Home. Starting, resetting or setting the countdown dismisses it
too.

**Other alerts still get through.** A Claude alert or a meeting about to
start shows over it for its few seconds, then the countdown's words come
back. A countdown that reaches zero during one of them now shows once that
alert is done, instead of being missed.

**Installing for the first time?** Drag `wef-notch.app` into Applications with
the Finder before you open it. Opened from Downloads first, macOS runs it from
a hidden copy: it can't launch at login or update. The README's *Build and
install* says how to put that right.
]]></description>
