            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[# wef-notch 0.6.0

**Every item within reach.** When the To-do list holds more than the card
shows, click **+N more** to turn to the next page; the last page has
**‹ Back** to the first. The card is back on its first page each time the
Panel opens.

**Edit an item in place.** Double-click an item's text to change it: the
text turns into a field, all of it selected. Return saves, Escape keeps what
was there, and a click anywhere else saves too. To tick an item, click its
circle; a click on the text alone does nothing, so nothing moves under a
double-click.

**When you added it.** On the To-do tab each item shows when it was added,
like `10 Nov 14:30`, beside its ×. Items added before this version show no
time.

**A full list says so.** At 20 items the field reads **List full (20)** and
Add dims, instead of quietly doing nothing.

**Installing for the first time?** Drag `wef-notch.app` into Applications with
the Finder before you open it. Opened from Downloads first, macOS runs it from
a hidden copy: it can't launch at login or update. The README's *Build and
install* says how to put that right.

]]></description>
